usage: wiki [-h] COMMAND ...

Personal wiki over my coding-class projects, powered by local Gemma (offline).

positional arguments:
  COMMAND
    ingest    read sources, generate linked wiki notes, update the index
    reindex   rebuild the search index from vault/raw (no model needed)
    check     check the vault: broken links, headings, note names, duplicates
    search    show original matching passages and paths (no answer generated)
    ask       standalone factual answer with citations, or 'insufficient
              evidence'
    chat      personal assistant; uses conversation context, looks up notes
              when useful
    status    show model, execution mode and whether the local model is ready

options:
  -h, --help  show this help message and exit

examples:
  wiki ingest ./vault/raw
  wiki ingest ./vault/raw --force
  wiki reindex
  wiki check
  wiki search "row level security"
  wiki ask "What learning rate did I use for the Pac-Man DQN?" --mode local
  wiki chat
  wiki status

configuration (environment variables):
  WIKI_MODEL    local Ollama model      (default: gemma4:e2b-it-qat)
  OLLAMA_HOST   Ollama server address   (default: http://localhost:11434)
  WIKI_NUM_CTX  context window, tokens  (default: 8192)

required inputs:
  - Ollama running with the model pulled (ingest, ask, chat)
  - source files (.md or .txt) in vault/raw/
  - search needs only the index built by 'wiki ingest' or 'wiki reindex'; the model can be off
